 ## Background
-Simplex Noise was introduced by Stefan Gustavson, optimized by Peter Eastman, with a better rank ordering method from 2012 [S1, unofficial]. It was designed to address the limitations of Perlin Noise, specifically the directional artifacts and high computational cost in higher dimensions [S4, S11, unofficial]. It is widely used in procedural generation for terrain, textures, and volumetric effects in games and simulations [S2][S4, S5, unofficial].
